hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1298","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, Abd al-Samad told me, Omar bin Sulayman told us, he used to stay in Banu Qusayr, Abu al-Walid told me, he said: I said: To Ibn Omar: What is the origin of this pebble in the mosque? He said: It rained during the night, so we came to the mosque to pray. He said: So the man carried pebbles in his clothes and threw them and prayed over them. In the morning, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “What is this?” So they informed him, and he said: “What a beautiful rug this is.” He said: So the people took it. He said: I said: What was the beginning of this saffron? He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to perform the morning prayer, and he saw a dent in the qibla of the mosque. He scratched it and said: “How ugly it is.” “This.” He said: Then the man who had soaked his hair came and rubbed it, then daubed saffron on it. He said: “This is better than that.” He said: I said: What’s the matter? When one of us relieves himself, he looks at her when he gets up? He said: “The king says to him: Look at what you have done with him and what has happened.”"
